_url":"https://api.github.com/users/semantic-release-bot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/semantic-release-bot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/semantic-release-bot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/semantic-release-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/semantic-release-bot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/semantic-release-bot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adobe/aem-experimentation/commits/72450908358c0c80b2468d8cc614ea0b85ba21d6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T18:45:46Z","email":"semantic-release-bot@martynus.net","name":"semantic-release-bot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T18:45:46Z","email":"semantic-release-bot@martynus.net","name":"semantic-release-bot"},"message":"chore(release): 1.2.2 [skip ci]\n\n## [1.2.2](https://github.com/adobe/aem-experimentation/compare/v1.2.1...v1.2.2) (2026-08-12)\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n* resolve multi-word audience/campaign names at page level ([#65](https://github.com/adobe/aem-experimentation/issues/65)) ([3fa2579](https://github.com/adobe/aem-experimentation/commit/3fa2579ac5e2bb0c638e0a8a5a2af90ba48c059d))","tree":{"sha":"5555a66d586ebe59d388446759b96a5694d9dfe2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adobe/aem-experimentation/git/trees/5555a66d586ebe59d388446759b96a5694d9dfe2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adobe/aem-experimentation/git/commits/72450908358c0c80b2468d8cc614ea0b85ba21d6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32174276?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/semantic-release-bot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/semantic-release-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/semantic-release-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/semantic-release-bot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/semantic-release-bot","id":32174276,"login":"semantic-release-bot","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMTc0Mjc2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/semantic-release-bot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/semantic-release-bot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/semantic-release-bot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/semantic-release-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/semantic-release-bot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/semantic-release-bot","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/adobe/aem-experimentation/commit/72450908358c0c80b2468d8cc614ea0b85ba21d6","node_id":"C_kwDOKK7qHNoAKDcyNDUwOTA4MzU4YzBjODBiMjQ2OGQ4Y2M2MTRlYTBiODViYTIxZDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/adobe/aem-experimentation/commit/3fa2579ac5e2bb0c638e0a8a5a2af90ba48c059d","sha":"3fa2579ac5e2bb0c638e0a8a5a2af90ba48c059d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adobe/aem-experimentation/commits/3fa2579ac5e2bb0c638e0a8a5a2af90ba48c059d"}],"sha":"72450908358c0c80b2468d8cc614ea0b85ba21d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adobe/aem-experimentation/commits/72450908358c0c80b2468d8cc614ea0b85ba21d6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1235810?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramboz/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramboz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramboz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramboz/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ramboz","id":1235810,"login":"ramboz","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMzU4MTA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramboz/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramboz/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramboz/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramboz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramboz/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramboz","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adobe/aem-experimentation/commits/3fa2579ac5e2bb0c638e0a8a5a2af90ba48c059d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T18:45:04Z","email":"ramboz@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Julien Ramboz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T18:45:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: resolve multi-word audience/campaign names at page level (#65)\n\n## Problem\n\nA **page-level** audience or campaign with a **multi-word name** (e.g.\n`returning-visitor`, `black-friday`) resolves its *membership* but never\nserves the variant — the experience is silently dropped.\n\nRoot cause: page-level metadata is read with `getAllMetadata`, which\n**camelCases** keys (`audience-returning-visitor` → `returningVisitor`).\nNames are then matched + looked up in **class-name** form, and\n`toClassName(''returningVisitor'')` → `returningvisitor` (the word\nboundary is lost), so it matches neither the project config key\n(`returning-visitor`) nor the camelCase one. Section- and fragment-level\nalready key names by class-name, so they work — only page-level is\naffected.\n\n## Fix\n\n- `getAllMetadata(scope, keyFn = toCamelCase)` — an optional key\ntransform. The default is unchanged, so **experiments keep their\ncamelCased config props** (`startDate`, `requiresConsent`, …).\n- `applyAllModifications` passes `toClassName` for **audience/campaign**\npage metadata (experiments keep `toCamelCase`), matching how section-\nand fragment-level already read names.\n- Config readers (`getAudienceConfig` / `getCampaignConfig`) are\n**unchanged** — they already handle class-name keys.\n\n## Tests\n\nAdds page-level fixtures + tests for a multi-word audience and a\nmulti-word campaign name. They fail red before this change (the variant\nisn''t served) and pass after. **Full suite green — 101 tests, including\nexperiments — no regression.**\n\n---\n\nFound while building a bring-your-own-engine integration (see #64) —\nthis is bug #2 from that RFC. It removes the need for hyphen-free tokens\nat page level.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5de21a0c776d883f7422220ba2872509332152dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adobe/aem-experimentation/git/trees/5de21a0c776d883f7422220ba2872509332152dd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adobe/aem-experimentation/git/commits/3fa2579ac5e2bb0c638e0a8a5a2af90ba48c059d","verification":{"payload":"tree 5de21a0c776d883f7422220ba2872509332152dd\nparent 6d50ecd00a92a1f275fb6e8de1cf7273491be950\nauthor Julien Ramboz <ramboz@users.noreply.github.com> 1786560304 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786560304 -0700\n\nfix: resolve multi-word audience/campaign names at page level (#65)\n\n## Problem\n\nA **page-level** audience or campaign with a **multi-word name** (e.g.\n`returning-visitor`, `black-friday`) resolves its *membership* but never\nserves the variant — the experience is silently dropped.\n\nRoot cause: page-level metadata is read with `getAllMetadata`, which\n**camelCases** keys (`audience-returning-visitor` → `returningVisitor`).\nNames are then matched + looked up in **class-name** form, and\n`toClassName(''returningVisitor'')` → `returningvisitor` (the word\nboundary is lost), so it matches neither the project config key\n(`returning-visitor`) nor the camelCase one. Section- and fragment-level\nalready key names by class-name, so they work — only page-level is\naffected.\n\n## Fix\n\n- `getAllMetadata(scope, keyFn = toCamelCase)` — an optional key\ntransform. The default is unchanged, so **experiments keep their\ncamelCased config props** (`startDate`, `requiresConsent`, …).\n- `applyAllModifications` passes `toClassName` for **audience/campaign**\npage metadata (experiments keep `toCamelCase`), matching how section-\nand fragment-level already read names.\n- Config readers (`getAudienceConfig` / `getCampaignConfig`) are\n**unchanged** — they already handle class-name keys.\n\n## Tests\n\nAdds page-level fixtures + tests for a multi-word audience and a\nmulti-word campaign name. They fail red before this change (the variant\nisn''t served) and pass after. **Full suite green — 101 tests, including\nexperiments — no regression.**\n\n---\n\nFound while building a bring-your-own-engine integration (see #64) —\nthis is bug #2 from that RFC. It removes the need for hyphen-free tokens\nat page level.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfL8wCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZZsQAEOQ97VA5U88dNL7+UV4M96X\nSqsE5cEOmPvxY2+ypC7DDtDmBylhVhMZYFtEnfPqJ1K2ltwIyL7/iF9fA6x3CGgl\nD95NTTu1HkTIHufEh7tmMgZQs98oJ5Ka3WUtJagn9Tea80m8J3rPx0jLaYn19b4n\nGdkLOw+e7V9AN9igXGFjZ1W/DwsLeKAUWVsZIVP2ktAlsCmhrH14UwnkqJT56A6A\n6cWrsH/kecbBIoXLrLVSZ+3yOdGzyvkppZ3d8uuRImIiB5dSVbImc0SOSYv64JZl\n3v0oLeA/PKdx5IlFfAAoZkoEHxCHmA0NwCElrk5EtnU1qn2c08YRpuDhgoOBdVaA\nRxgSLXBAdncrDIQkN9CLOuuyij1HkNjIett6sH5yZl9S2BKcJV7JX7GsAWsXET0n\nqzW07/YAxpOfXsG6KV6ENtyM13FGhmuyga2pNd2U5AB0TtkmU0nbaI5CWFmnZHl5\nb9YIxUWQ4xuQGA/0dYz/bljA9Id6wWTclCgxauDt8yzXc0uRZOuAfoJhf0FnvDuh\nWp8rj29OXQUM5D2t82HkPzim5CdkvfYMTr0xhZ7rm1NL1NVPs2Ny1FPXOzI8JhRy\nPcCjJ0T33Jn9jHAHb2S6m0V0hM7j+X8tmupnGB6q7Ie6hr2aCveQaIsqBFtkVWt8\njDmeMqdB9cLGXt4D+aOt\n=u2jy\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-12T18:45:08Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","follow