tps://api.github.com/users/semantic-release-bot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/semantic-release-bot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/semantic-release-bot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/semantic-release-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/semantic-release-bot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/semantic-release-bot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adobe/aem-experimentation/commits/6d50ecd00a92a1f275fb6e8de1cf7273491be950/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T16:44:50Z","email":"semantic-release-bot@martynus.net","name":"semantic-release-bot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T16:44:50Z","email":"semantic-release-bot@martynus.net","name":"semantic-release-bot"},"message":"chore(release): 1.2.1 [skip ci]\n\n## [1.2.1](https://github.com/adobe/aem-experimentation/compare/v1.2.0...v1.2.1) (2026-08-12)\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n* support a single audience/campaign per selector in fragment manifests ([#63](https://github.com/adobe/aem-experimentation/issues/63)) ([6f7b3e8](https://github.com/adobe/aem-experimentation/commit/6f7b3e8c382dcbb5750d58025db2a46ccd6e612e))","tree":{"sha":"0cd292f7c97c83158b04413cfb8c730d8b4ea9e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adobe/aem-experimentation/git/trees/0cd292f7c97c83158b04413cfb8c730d8b4ea9e1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adobe/aem-experimentation/git/commits/6d50ecd00a92a1f275fb6e8de1cf7273491be950","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32174276?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/semantic-release-bot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/semantic-release-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/semantic-release-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/semantic-release-bot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/semantic-release-bot","id":32174276,"login":"semantic-release-bot","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMTc0Mjc2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/semantic-release-bot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/semantic-release-bot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/semantic-release-bot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/semantic-release-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/semantic-release-bot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/semantic-release-bot","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/adobe/aem-experimentation/commit/6d50ecd00a92a1f275fb6e8de1cf7273491be950","node_id":"C_kwDOKK7qHNoAKDZkNTBlY2QwMGE5MmExZjI3NWZiNmU4ZGUxY2Y3MjczNDkxYmU5NTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/adobe/aem-experimentation/commit/6f7b3e8c382dcbb5750d58025db2a46ccd6e612e","sha":"6f7b3e8c382dcbb5750d58025db2a46ccd6e612e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adobe/aem-experimentation/commits/6f7b3e8c382dcbb5750d58025db2a46ccd6e612e"}],"sha":"6d50ecd00a92a1f275fb6e8de1cf7273491be950","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adobe/aem-experimentation/commits/6d50ecd00a92a1f275fb6e8de1cf7273491be950"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1235810?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramboz/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramboz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramboz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramboz/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ramboz","id":1235810,"login":"ramboz","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMzU4MTA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramboz/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramboz/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramboz/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramboz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramboz/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramboz","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adobe/aem-experimentation/commits/6f7b3e8c382dcbb5750d58025db2a46ccd6e612e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T16:44:13Z","email":"ramboz@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Julien Ramboz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T16:44:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: support a single audience/campaign per selector in fragment manifests (#63)\n\n## Problem\n\nA fragment-level **Audience Manifest** (or **Campaign Manifest**) with a\n**single audience/campaign per selector** crashes the plugin.\n\n`parseAudienceManifest` / `parseCampaignManifest` call\n`audiences.forEach(...)` / `campaigns.forEach(...)`, but\n`aggregateEntries` only produces an **array** when a selector has\n*multiple* values — a selector with a single value leaves\n`audience`/`campaign` (and `url`) as a **scalar string**.\n`String.prototype.forEach` doesn''t exist, so it throws\n`audiences.forEach is not a function`, which aborts `loadEager` and\nleaves the fragment un-personalized (`window.hlx.audiences` /\n`.campaigns` never gets set).\n\nEvery existing manifest fixture uses *two* audiences/campaigns per\nselector, so this single-value path was never exercised.\n\n## Fix\n\nNormalize `audience`/`campaign` and `url` to arrays with\n`[].concat(...)` before iterating — a no-op for the existing multi-value\ncase, correct for the single-value case.\n\n## Tests\n\nAdds fragment-level fixtures + tests for a **single audience** and a\n**single campaign** per selector. They fail red before this change\n(`waitForNamespace` times out because the plugin threw) and pass after.\nFull `audiences` + `campaigns` suites green (**46 passed**), lint clean.\n\n---\n\nFound while building a \"bring your own decision engine\" personalization\nintegration, where each slot''s manifest carries exactly one (remote)\naudience — a common shape for per-slot personalization, so it''s worth\nhandling out of the box.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e2eb25a0617e118dc38b7d901515c50e31a363d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adobe/aem-experimentation/git/trees/e2eb25a0617e118dc38b7d901515c50e31a363d0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adobe/aem-experimentation/git/commits/6f7b3e8c382dcbb5750d58025db2a46ccd6e612e","verification":{"payload":"tree e2eb25a0617e118dc38b7d901515c50e31a363d0\nparent 11caa14727262dac1e4ca6a7c888717485ba13c4\nauthor Julien Ramboz <ramboz@users.noreply.github.com> 1786553053 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786553053 -0700\n\nfix: support a single audience/campaign per selector in fragment manifests (#63)\n\n## Problem\n\nA fragment-level **Audience Manifest** (or **Campaign Manifest**) with a\n**single audience/campaign per selector** crashes the plugin.\n\n`parseAudienceManifest` / `parseCampaignManifest` call\n`audiences.forEach(...)` / `campaigns.forEach(...)`, but\n`aggregateEntries` only produces an **array** when a selector has\n*multiple* values — a selector with a single value leaves\n`audience`/`campaign` (and `url`) as a **scalar string**.\n`String.prototype.forEach` doesn''t exist, so it throws\n`audiences.forEach is not a function`, which aborts `loadEager` and\nleaves the fragment un-personalized (`window.hlx.audiences` /\n`.campaigns` never gets set).\n\nEvery existing manifest fixture uses *two* audiences/campaigns per\nselector, so this single-value path was never exercised.\n\n## Fix\n\nNormalize `audience`/`campaign` and `url` to arrays with\n`[].concat(...)` before iterating — a no-op for the existing multi-value\ncase, correct for the single-value case.\n\n## Tests\n\nAdds fragment-level fixtures + tests for a **single audience** and a\n**single campaign** per selector. They fail red before this change\n(`waitForNamespace` times out because the plugin threw) and pass after.\nFull `audiences` + `campaigns` suites green (**46 passed**), lint clean.\n\n---\n\nFound while building a \"bring your own decision engine\" personalization\nintegration, where each slot''s manifest carries exactly one (remote)\naudience — a common shape for per-slot personalization, so it''s worth\nhandling out of the box.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfKLdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACkQQAEKIv25PiiRTogCrUKPc0rfr\nf6Tv6i8w/MEDRjO1r4o/VQmpPSh7G+9HboXlhxLodrznbroLfU2taGfHFdBpA19T\nE4DLtEaVcfOKij97KHp9CMw0cHAhsRylZy2ldj2PYeGyyOmFf++PWjV6aISe2GQp\nPNlfCR75iWIhsesS2Zi4g0lidYWx+BKDZuNolIap49BzNHPjD8UsEkA6Bs1ndim6\n7S0MUHnO5WkqsoyOb3zdGErueWFVPshMZV5/rLoEzFHym+rtd5up/vEYZNpxs8HA\nY6AkDEHhWdqrcFKllcT/JHuvAStmS79QAutzly17Xb18P6h/mn8/TNp9DXOAn2Vl\nr/eBLHFSmvlvX/xK1c+fP5Tjjpsq79VpCqX+w87Q3+/sCJT7Mk37vlhNW///pbKH\nZXmVz2d/nk6wCKV/+Bil3G1a6cn4s0LfwIPJkuk9g8jkznznArepREZS+bE+ftXu\n3yccqV1piy3ZjMlw1WrE6M5ZKot1vapqsIJPwwi/ZILJQbsPLONm42u+bxGhX2D1\nSRWJfec7gvDSzwoF0EWbnzwsvZSc0m3JT8UdZdfNGSunbT+kg8NqFFD5VElJ4/dQ\nmlhOTlBtjbcx6QXJ+fIplJfKj01jFMVOKk8TRo8SLbh571JM44G9qdP6knO4s+IT\n3MQp4dY1/xqO38X3aTcH\n=r3w1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-12T16:44:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}